<title>GERMANY: Dresdner sees 96 earnings up at least 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Dresdner sees 96 earnings up at least 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Dresdner Bank AG on Thursday predicted a clear double-digit rise in earnings this year after its operating profits advanced by nearly a third in the first nine months.</p>
<p>A Dresdner statement said chief executive Juergen Sarrazin &quot;was expecting clear double digit growth in earnings for the full year.&quot;</p>
<p>The bank's operating profit rose 29.7 percent to 1.89 billion marks in the first nine months of 1996, in the range of analysts' expectations.</p>
</text>
